{"key": "averitec/dev/2", "dataset": "averitec", "split": "dev", "original_index": 2, "claim": "Due to Imran Khan's criticism of Macron's comments on Islam, French authorities cancelled the visas of 183 Pakistani citizens and deported 118 from the country.", "claim_date": "31-10-2020", "gold_label": "Refuted", "results": {"hero2": {"status": "ok", "predicted_label": "Not Enough Evidence", "label_correct": false, "qa_pairs": [{"question": "What is the connection between Imran Khan's criticism of President Macron and the cancellation of visas and deportation of Pakistani citizens by French authorities?", "answer": "Based on the provided evidence, there is no connection mentioned between Imran Khan's criticism of President Macron and the cancellation of visas or the deportation of Pakistani citizens.\n\nThe evidence states that Imran Khan accused President Macron of attacking Islam and encouraging Islamophobia following Macron's defense of cartoons depicting the Prophet Mohammed. While this led to tensions and calls for boycotts of French goods in several Muslim countries, the text does not contain any information regarding French authorities cancelling visas for 183 Pakistani citizens or deporting 118 individuals.", "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/pakistans-pm-imran-khan-accuses-french-president-macron-of-attacking-islam/articleshow/78859784.cms", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}, {"question": "What was the reason for the diplomatic tension between Pakistan and France?", "answer": "The diplomatic tension between Pakistan and France was caused by controversial remarks made by French President Emmanuel Macron regarding Islam and blasphemy. Specifically, the tension escalated after Macron defended the right to blaspheme and referred to a slain schoolteacher as a \"quiet hero.\" In response, Pakistani Prime Minister Imran Khan criticized the President, accusing him of encouraging polarization and Islamophobia rather than addressing extremism. Pakistan expressed deep concern over what it described as \"systematic Islamophobic acts\" following these comments.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2020/10/26/pakistan-accuses-macron-of-encouraging", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}, {"question": "Does the evidence support the claim that French authorities cancelled visas and deported Pakistani citizens in response to Imran Khan's criticism of President Macron?", "answer": "No, the evidence does not support the claim.\n\nThe provided text states that Imran Khan criticized President Macron for defending the right to display cartoons of the Prophet Muhammad and that this criticism sparked boycotts of French goods. However, the evidence contains no mention of French authorities cancelling visas for 183 Pakistani citizens or deporting 118 individuals in response to his comments.", "url": "https://www.bbc.com/news/world-asia-54689283", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}, {"question": "Did French authorities cancel visas and deport Pakistani citizens as a direct consequence of Imran Khan's criticism of President Macron?", "answer": "Based on the provided evidence, there is no information to support the claim that French authorities cancelled the visas of 183 Pakistani citizens or deported 118 people as a consequence of Imran Khan's criticism.\n\nThe evidence confirms that tensions escalated between France and Pakistan due to President Macron's stance on freedom of expression and Prime Minister Imran Khan's criticism of the French president, but it does not mention any visa cancellations or deportations of Pakistani citizens.", "url": "https://www.euronews.com/2020/10/27/watch-live-macron-s-islam-comments-spark-protests-in-pakistani-city-of-karachi", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}, {"question": "Is there evidence in the provided text to support the claim that French authorities cancelled visas and deported Pakistani citizens in response to Imran Khan's criticism?", "answer": "No, there is no evidence in the provided text to support the claim that French authorities cancelled the visas of 183 Pakistani citizens or deported 118 people in response to Imran Khan's criticism. The text only mentions Khan's criticism of President Macron's defense of satirical caricatures and his call for Facebook to ban Islamophobic content.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/pakistans-imran-khan-slams-french-president-macrons-views-on-islam/a-55394035", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}, {"question": "Does the evidence provide any information regarding the cancellation of visas for Pakistani citizens or the deportation of individuals by French authorities in response to Imran Khan's comments?", "answer": "No, the provided evidence does not contain any information regarding the cancellation of visas for Pakistani citizens or the deportation of individuals by French authorities. The evidence focuses exclusively on an incident involving Imran Khan being detained and interrogated by US immigration officials in Toronto related to his opposition to American drone strikes.", "url": "https://www.france24.com/en/20121027-usa-immigration-officials-question-pakistan-politician-imran-khan-drone-air-strikes", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}, {"question": "Does the provided evidence support the claim that French authorities cancelled visas and deported Pakistani citizens due to Imran Khan's criticism of Macron?", "answer": "No, the provided evidence does not support the claim.\n\nThe evidence consists solely of a collection of user comments reacting to a video about Taslima Nasrin's statements. The text contains no information regarding Imran Khan, President Macron, visa cancellations, or the deportation of Pakistani citizens.", "url": "https://www.facebook.com/abplive/posts/heres-what-taslima-nasrin-said-on-france-terror-attack-l-abp-uncut/5165726253445357/", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}, {"question": "What is the relationship between the actions taken by French authorities and the deportation measures implemented by the Indian government?", "answer": "Based on the provided evidence, there is no relationship mentioned between the actions taken by French authorities and the deportation measures implemented by the Indian government.\n\nThe evidence focuses exclusively on the Indian government's response to the influx of illegal immigrants in the North East region, detailing instructions to state governments regarding deportation proceedings and the cancellation of fraudulent identification. The evidence does not contain any information regarding French authorities or their actions related to Pakistani citizens.", "url": "https://www.facebook.com/themorningbellnewspaper/posts/states-advised-to-initiate-deportation-of-illegal-immigrants-govtno-accurate-cen/362988110932947/", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}, {"question": "Does the evidence provided support the claim regarding the cancellation of visas and deportation of Pakistani citizens by French authorities?", "answer": "No, the evidence provided does not support the claim. The provided text discusses changes to the Merchant Discount Rate (MDR) for UPI payments in India, and contains no information regarding Imran Khan, French authorities, visa cancellations, or the deportation of Pakistani citizens.", "url": "https://www.facebook.com/cnbctv18india/videos/pak-pm-imran-khan-accuses-french-president-macron-of-attacking-islam/990217951480998/", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}, {"question": "Did the criticism by Imran Khan regarding Macron's comments on Islam lead French authorities to cancel the visas of 183 Pakistani citizens and deport 118 of them?", "answer": "Based on the evidence provided, it is not possible to determine whether Imran Khan's criticism led to the cancellation of visas or the deportation of Pakistani citizens. The provided text focuses exclusively on the political fragmentation, military developments, and humanitarian crisis in Yemen during 2019 and does not contain any information regarding Imran Khan, President Macron, or French immigration policies concerning Pakistani citizens.", "url": "https://sanaacenter.org/publications/the-yemen-review/8923", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}], "justification": "To determine the verdict for the claim, we evaluate the provided evidence through the following steps:\n\n1.  **Analyze the Claim:** The claim asserts a specific causal link: Imran Khan's criticism of President Macron's comments on Islam directly resulted in French authorities cancelling 183 Pakistani visas and deporting 118 Pakistani citizens.\n\n2.  **Evaluate the Evidence (Q&A Pairs):**\n    *   **Q1, Q3, Q4, Q5:** These answers explicitly state that while the evidence confirms the diplomatic tension and Imran Khan's criticism of Macron, there is **no mention** of visa cancellations or deportations in the text.\n    *   **Q6:** Notes that the evidence actually discusses an unrelated incident involving Imran Khan in Toronto.\n    *   **Q7:** States the evidence consists of user comments about Taslima Nasrin and contains no information regarding the claim.\n    *   **Q8:** Discusses Indian government deportation measures, which is irrelevant to the claim about France.\n    *   **Q9:** Discusses UPI payments in India, which is irrelevant.\n    *   **Q10:** Discusses the humanitarian crisis in Yemen, which is irrelevant.\n\n3.  **Synthesize Findings:** Across all provided question-answer pairs, the evidence is either explicitly negative (stating the information is not present) or entirely irrelevant to the subject matter (discussing Yemen, India, or UPI payments). There is no data provided that confirms the specific numbers (183 visas, 118 deportations) or the causal link described in the claim.\n\n4.  **Determine the Label:** Since the provided evidence does not contain the information necessary to prove or disprove the specific details of the claim (the numbers and the specific action taken by French authorities), the correct classification is that there is insufficient information.\n\n**Label: Not Enough Evidence**", "admitted_sources": [{"url": "https://www.facebook.com/abplive/posts/heres-what-taslima-nasrin-said-on-france-terror-attack-l-abp-uncut/5165726253445357/", "date": "2016-02-02", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://sanaacenter.org/publications/the-yemen-review/8923", "date": "2020-01-30", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://dokumen.pub/persian-miniatures-inside-the-islamic-republic-of-iran-2002-2020.html", "date": "2002-01-01", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://www.dw.com/en/pakistans-imran-khan-slams-french-president-macrons-views-on-islam/a-55394035", "date": "2020-10-25", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2020/10/26/pakistan-accuses-macron-of-encouraging", "date": "2020-10-26", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://www.bbc.com/news/world-asia-54689283", "date": "2020-10-26", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://www.facebook.com/cnbctv18india/videos/pak-pm-imran-khan-accuses-french-president-macron-of-attacking-islam/990217951480998/", "date": "2020-10-26", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://www.euronews.com/2020/10/27/watch-live-macron-s-islam-comments-spark-protests-in-pakistani-city-of-karachi